1
00:01:30,990 --> 00:01:33,990
Laios and crew are returning to the surface.

2
00:01:33,990 --> 00:01:35,990
I just don't want to lose any of you.

3
00:01:35,990 --> 00:01:37,990
Me neither.

4
00:01:37,990 --> 00:01:40,990
While their bonds are growing ever stronger,

5
00:01:40,990 --> 00:01:43,990
let's go back in time a bit.

6
00:01:44,990 --> 00:01:47,990
You're finally conscious.

7
00:01:47,990 --> 00:01:49,990
Are you feeling all right?

8
00:01:49,990 --> 00:01:52,990
Your injuries weren't too severe.

9
00:01:52,990 --> 00:01:55,990
I had to use goat's blood to replace what you lost.

10
00:01:55,990 --> 00:01:58,990
It'll do for now, but you should return to town soon.

11
00:01:59,990 --> 00:02:01,990
It's good you weren't still in the water,

12
00:02:01,990 --> 00:02:03,990
or you'd have been fish food.

13
00:02:03,990 --> 00:02:06,990
You should be thankful to whoever pulled you out.

14
00:02:06,990 --> 00:02:08,990
Are you thinking what I am?

15
00:02:08,990 --> 00:02:09,990
Kuro!

16
00:02:12,990 --> 00:02:14,990
I know this scent.

17
00:02:14,990 --> 00:02:20,990
Elf. Tall man. Half foot. Dwarf.

18
00:02:20,990 --> 00:02:22,990
The ones who stole our treasure.

19
00:02:22,990 --> 00:02:24,990
I had a feeling it was those guys!

20
00:02:24,990 --> 00:02:29,990
The revival fee, please.

21
00:02:29,990 --> 00:02:32,990
Enough for the goat's blood is fine.

22
00:02:33,990 --> 00:02:34,990
That's right.

23
00:02:34,990 --> 00:02:35,990
We were...

24
00:02:35,990 --> 00:02:38,990
Assaulted by some fishmen.

25
00:02:38,990 --> 00:02:47,990
I guess we must have died again.

26
00:02:47,990 --> 00:02:49,990
This is plenty, thank you.

27
00:02:49,990 --> 00:02:52,990
They're adventurers?

28
00:02:54,990 --> 00:02:56,990
Aren't you...

29
00:02:56,990 --> 00:02:58,990
Need something?

30
00:02:58,990 --> 00:02:59,990
No.

31
00:02:59,990 --> 00:03:01,990
Let's go, Nomari.

32
00:03:01,990 --> 00:03:02,990
Right!

33
00:03:06,990 --> 00:03:08,990
Got a soft spot for dwarves?

34
00:03:08,990 --> 00:03:09,990
Hm?

35
00:03:09,990 --> 00:03:10,990
You have no integrity.

36
00:03:10,990 --> 00:03:14,990
Hey, I don't use someone's height to determine whether or not I hang out with them.

37
00:03:14,990 --> 00:03:16,990
That's so.

38
00:03:16,990 --> 00:03:18,990
Our food is gone!

39
00:03:18,990 --> 00:03:20,990
It got stolen by those guys again!

40
00:03:20,990 --> 00:03:21,990
Food.

41
00:03:21,990 --> 00:03:23,990
Are you kidding me?!

42
00:03:23,990 --> 00:03:24,990
It's so weird.

43
00:03:24,990 --> 00:03:27,990
They always take all our food, but none of our money.

44
00:03:27,990 --> 00:03:29,990
Maybe they keep running out of it?

45
00:03:29,990 --> 00:03:31,990
So annoying.

46
00:03:31,990 --> 00:03:33,990
We really should teach them a lesson.

47
00:03:33,990 --> 00:03:35,990
What's the plan, Kabru?

48
00:03:35,990 --> 00:03:36,990
Hmm.

49
00:03:36,990 --> 00:03:38,990
There's no choice.

50
00:03:38,990 --> 00:03:39,990
Let's go back.

51
00:03:39,990 --> 00:03:40,990
Wait!

52
00:03:40,990 --> 00:03:41,990
You're joking, right?

53
00:03:41,990 --> 00:03:42,990
Shouldn't we go after them?

54
00:03:42,990 --> 00:03:44,990
We don't have any food, though.

55
00:03:44,990 --> 00:03:46,990
So we shouldn't go any further.

56
00:03:46,990 --> 00:03:49,990
How about we admit defeat for now?

57
00:03:49,990 --> 00:03:54,990
Like that guy said before he left, we have to be thankful that we're alive at all.

58
00:03:56,990 --> 00:03:59,990
If that's what you want to do, I guess I'll stick with you.

59
00:03:59,990 --> 00:04:00,990
I will, too.

60
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:05,990
If you promise you won't give up on finding those filthy criminals, then I'm fine to return.

61
00:04:05,990 --> 00:04:07,990
I promise, Ren. Thanks.

62
00:04:08,990 --> 00:04:10,990
Koro will do what Mikbel does.

63
00:04:12,990 --> 00:04:13,990
Oh, man.

64
00:04:14,990 --> 00:04:17,990
I can't believe we're not making any profit this time.

65
00:04:19,990 --> 00:04:26,990
There's so much fog.

66
00:04:26,990 --> 00:04:28,990
Hey, be careful, everyone!

67
00:04:32,990 --> 00:04:36,990
This fog didn't occur naturally.

68
00:04:36,990 --> 00:04:38,990
It's from a monster.

69
00:04:38,990 --> 00:04:45,990
A fish man?

70
00:04:45,990 --> 00:04:50,990
There are so many of them.

71
00:04:50,990 --> 00:04:53,990
I guess there's no choice.

72
00:04:53,990 --> 00:04:55,990
Come on!

73
00:04:55,990 --> 00:05:05,990
The way it uses that axe seems familiar.

74
00:05:05,990 --> 00:05:07,990
This swinging motion.

75
00:05:07,990 --> 00:05:09,990
I know it all too well.

76
00:05:10,990 --> 00:05:11,990
That's right.

77
00:05:11,990 --> 00:05:12,990
This is...

78
00:05:18,990 --> 00:05:19,990
Shh.

79
00:05:19,990 --> 00:05:20,990
Everything's fine.

80
00:05:20,990 --> 00:05:21,990
Just calm down.

81
00:05:21,990 --> 00:05:22,990
Daya.

82
00:05:22,990 --> 00:05:23,990
It's me.

83
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:28,990
This fog's illusion magic.

84
00:05:28,990 --> 00:05:32,990
The confused one with their weapon drawn is Koro.

85
00:05:32,990 --> 00:05:35,990
And the one zoning out across from him is home.

86
00:05:35,990 --> 00:05:38,990
He has a habit of freezing up when things get a bit crazy.

87
00:05:38,990 --> 00:05:41,990
The one who ran off is probably Mik.

88
00:05:42,990 --> 00:05:45,990
So, the one that poses the most dangerous...

89
00:05:46,990 --> 00:05:47,990
Ren.

90
00:05:47,990 --> 00:05:49,990
She's already in mid-chant.

91
00:05:50,990 --> 00:05:53,990
She has the power to turn us all into ashes instantly.

92
00:05:54,990 --> 00:05:57,990
The only peaceful way to stop a chanting magic user is...

93
00:05:57,990 --> 00:05:58,990
Ren.

94
00:05:58,990 --> 00:05:59,990
You get it, right?

95
00:05:59,990 --> 00:06:00,990
This is all an illusion.

96
00:06:00,990 --> 00:06:01,990
It's too bad she looks like a monster.

97
00:06:01,990 --> 00:06:02,990
Now then.

98
00:06:02,990 --> 00:06:03,990
In order to stop this fog that was conjured...

99
00:06:03,990 --> 00:06:04,990
Huh.

100
00:06:04,990 --> 00:06:19,990
This isn't the right one.

101
00:06:26,990 --> 00:06:28,990
This isn't the right one.

102
00:06:28,990 --> 00:06:31,990
Those who attack with weapons aren't casters.

103
00:06:31,990 --> 00:06:34,890
They're always observing things from afar.

104
00:06:36,030 --> 00:06:36,870
That one.

105
00:06:49,990 --> 00:06:51,950
All right, all right.

106
00:06:52,110 --> 00:06:52,770
We surrender.

107
00:06:53,710 --> 00:06:56,010
So would you mind letting go of my mage friend?

108
00:06:56,770 --> 00:06:57,850
Wait a minute.

109
00:06:58,370 --> 00:07:00,510
They're the corpse retrievers from upstairs.

110
00:07:00,510 --> 00:07:03,810
I don't think this reunion is just a coincidence.

111
00:07:04,390 --> 00:07:05,710
You guys followed us, right?

112
00:07:06,150 --> 00:07:07,350
What do you mean?

113
00:07:07,810 --> 00:07:10,990
It's more profitable to retrieve corpses from a deeper floor,

114
00:07:11,410 --> 00:07:13,030
because the island pays more for it.

115
00:07:14,090 --> 00:07:16,330
We were angry about our stuff being stolen.

116
00:07:16,810 --> 00:07:18,130
And while we were trying to get back,

117
00:07:18,370 --> 00:07:20,350
we went to a floor that was above our skill level.

118
00:07:21,090 --> 00:07:22,930
So all they had to do was follow us,

119
00:07:23,050 --> 00:07:25,050
and they would find more profitable corpses.

120
00:07:25,690 --> 00:07:27,930
Oh, so annoying.

121
00:07:27,930 --> 00:07:29,850
But you were a little too late.

122
00:07:30,510 --> 00:07:31,750
When you found us,

123
00:07:31,930 --> 00:07:33,670
we'd already been revived by someone else,

124
00:07:33,810 --> 00:07:35,370
and we were heading back to the surface.

125
00:07:36,050 --> 00:07:36,990
It made you panic.

126
00:07:37,350 --> 00:07:39,150
So you decided to use illusion magic

127
00:07:39,150 --> 00:07:40,670
to turn us all against each other.

128
00:07:41,030 --> 00:07:42,450
You're a little off base.

129
00:07:42,730 --> 00:07:45,550
What we wanted was for you to catch up to the thieves.

130
00:07:45,830 --> 00:07:48,430
Having you kill each other would have been the best scenario.

131
00:07:48,890 --> 00:07:50,290
But it's really a shame.

132
00:07:50,630 --> 00:07:52,290
We didn't think you'd die so quickly

133
00:07:52,290 --> 00:07:54,050
from being attacked by mere monsters.

134
00:07:54,050 --> 00:07:56,210
You're a little...

135
00:07:56,210 --> 00:07:59,690
Infighting and stealing between adventurers is a crime.

136
00:08:00,310 --> 00:08:02,110
I'm reporting you to the island lord.

137
00:08:04,190 --> 00:08:05,770
How about we make a deal?

138
00:08:06,410 --> 00:08:08,750
It'd be wasteful for you to go back empty-handed.

139
00:08:09,550 --> 00:08:12,710
Two of my party members were unfortunately taken out.

140
00:08:13,170 --> 00:08:15,050
Deliver them to the resurrection office.

141
00:08:15,510 --> 00:08:18,150
You should earn a decent amount of money for doing that.

142
00:08:18,150 --> 00:08:20,570
Those two were just unconscious.

143
00:08:23,050 --> 00:08:25,830
We'll testify that they got attacked by fishmen.

144
00:08:26,170 --> 00:08:27,730
As for splitting the reward,

145
00:08:28,230 --> 00:08:29,830
we're gonna take 40.

146
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:32,410
No, 30% of it.

147
00:08:32,910 --> 00:08:33,650
How's that?

148
00:08:33,810 --> 00:08:35,470
It's a pretty good deal, isn't it?

149
00:08:35,470 --> 00:08:39,170
All right.

150
00:08:39,550 --> 00:08:40,290
I'll do it.

151
00:08:42,470 --> 00:08:42,950
Kabru.

152
00:08:54,950 --> 00:08:56,590
Oh, damn you.

153
00:08:56,990 --> 00:08:58,450
Yeah, that makes more sense.

154
00:08:58,750 --> 00:09:00,150
I'm glad you did the right thing.

155
00:09:05,470 --> 00:09:14,290
Humanoids are so easy to deal with.

156
00:09:14,750 --> 00:09:16,750
Every single dwarf, gnome, and tallman,

157
00:09:16,930 --> 00:09:18,910
they all tend to have identical weak points.

158
00:09:19,170 --> 00:09:21,250
They move their bodies in the same way, too.

159
00:09:21,790 --> 00:09:23,990
It's too bad monsters aren't like that.

160
00:09:24,810 --> 00:09:27,190
Kuro, go find Mika, bring him back, will ya?

161
00:09:27,530 --> 00:09:27,790
Kuro!

162
00:09:28,690 --> 00:09:29,190
Kabru.

163
00:09:29,530 --> 00:09:29,710
Hmm?

164
00:09:29,710 --> 00:09:31,170
What about him?

165
00:09:31,310 --> 00:09:33,290
Please let me go, I swear to you!

166
00:09:33,290 --> 00:09:35,630
I didn't know about any of this!

167
00:09:36,590 --> 00:09:39,050
You don't aim to lift the dungeon's curse,

168
00:09:39,330 --> 00:09:41,390
nor eradicate the monsters in here.

169
00:09:42,170 --> 00:09:44,150
The number of people who make a living

170
00:09:44,150 --> 00:09:45,950
by stealing from others keeps growing.

171
00:09:46,630 --> 00:09:48,090
Good people from this island

172
00:09:48,090 --> 00:09:49,530
will leave if this continues.

173
00:09:52,010 --> 00:09:55,290
That's why I can't forgive people like you.

174
00:09:56,010 --> 00:09:56,790
Have mercy!

175
00:09:56,790 --> 00:10:16,290
Kabru?

176
00:10:16,710 --> 00:10:16,890
Hmm?

177
00:10:17,650 --> 00:10:19,450
Oh, sorry about earlier.

178
00:10:19,930 --> 00:10:21,830
It was the first solution I could think of.

179
00:10:22,470 --> 00:10:22,730
Hmm.

180
00:10:22,730 --> 00:10:24,710
What are you saying?

181
00:10:25,190 --> 00:10:25,870
You know what?

182
00:10:26,030 --> 00:10:26,650
Never mind.

183
00:10:26,970 --> 00:10:28,210
Okay, if you say so.

184
00:10:29,090 --> 00:10:30,430
I feel like we're messing up

185
00:10:30,430 --> 00:10:32,430
and not actually making any progress.

186
00:10:33,150 --> 00:10:33,770
You're right.

187
00:10:34,030 --> 00:10:35,850
And this is the result of all of that.

188
00:10:36,210 --> 00:10:37,410
It's really the worst.

189
00:10:38,030 --> 00:10:40,090
You could stand to be a bit more encouraging.

190
00:10:40,610 --> 00:10:42,310
There's no point in sugarcoating it.

191
00:10:42,670 --> 00:10:44,710
This is just the best we can do for right now.

192
00:10:44,710 --> 00:10:45,350
Huh.

193
00:10:46,130 --> 00:10:48,270
The Island Lord only sees this dungeon

194
00:10:48,270 --> 00:10:49,410
as a profitable tunnel.

195
00:10:50,170 --> 00:10:51,710
If the gold runs dry,

196
00:10:52,170 --> 00:10:53,930
he thinks that monster leather and bones

197
00:10:53,930 --> 00:10:54,670
would be enough.

198
00:10:55,310 --> 00:10:57,250
But no one's gonna dive into a dungeon

199
00:10:57,250 --> 00:10:58,810
that's been thoroughly searched through.

200
00:10:59,790 --> 00:11:02,410
Maybe because the get-rich-quick dream disappears,

201
00:11:03,050 --> 00:11:05,230
or the spirit of adventure isn't being met.

202
00:11:05,890 --> 00:11:07,690
The population starts to decline,

203
00:11:07,850 --> 00:11:09,310
and then...

204
00:11:09,310 --> 00:11:11,250
dangerous monsters pour out of the dungeon.

205
00:11:11,250 --> 00:11:14,970
That's how a countless number of towns

206
00:11:14,970 --> 00:11:15,890
have been destroyed.

207
00:11:16,970 --> 00:11:19,630
We have to lift this place's curse and fast.

208
00:11:20,270 --> 00:11:22,250
The world doesn't need monsters and dungeons.

209
00:11:22,970 --> 00:11:23,310
Yeah.

210
00:11:26,130 --> 00:11:27,070
I'm starving.

211
00:11:28,170 --> 00:11:30,130
Being revived does make you hungry, huh?

212
00:11:30,650 --> 00:11:31,130
Kabu!

213
00:11:31,430 --> 00:11:32,270
Check it out!

214
00:11:32,910 --> 00:11:33,850
Those guys were carrying

215
00:11:33,850 --> 00:11:35,430
some pretty valuable things on them!

216
00:11:35,870 --> 00:11:36,410
All right.

217
00:11:36,810 --> 00:11:38,110
Let's only take their food,

218
00:11:38,290 --> 00:11:39,710
and then sink the rest of it.

219
00:11:39,710 --> 00:11:41,370
What? Why sink it?

220
00:11:42,150 --> 00:11:44,330
If we take just everything,

221
00:11:44,530 --> 00:11:46,250
it means we're no better than they are.

222
00:11:47,090 --> 00:11:48,270
Once we're all finished,

223
00:11:48,470 --> 00:11:49,670
how about we eat a little something?

224
00:11:50,270 --> 00:11:51,210
Let's do it!

225
00:11:56,010 --> 00:11:57,830
It's time for us to dig in!

226
00:11:58,990 --> 00:11:59,470
Whoa!

227
00:11:59,930 --> 00:12:01,390
Those guys were eating good!

228
00:12:01,730 --> 00:12:03,930
I guess corpse retrievers get paid a lot.

229
00:12:04,110 --> 00:12:05,910
Yeah, when you're making your own corpses

230
00:12:05,910 --> 00:12:06,730
to take back.

231
00:12:06,730 --> 00:12:09,450
And the Island Lord hasn't caught on to that?

232
00:12:09,890 --> 00:12:11,230
There are actually inspections

233
00:12:11,230 --> 00:12:13,150
when it comes to payments from the island.

234
00:12:13,770 --> 00:12:15,090
But it seems like those guys

235
00:12:15,090 --> 00:12:16,070
were getting around it.

236
00:12:18,390 --> 00:12:19,790
It's honestly more likely

237
00:12:19,790 --> 00:12:21,030
that there are a lot of people

238
00:12:21,030 --> 00:12:22,690
working together behind the scenes.

239
00:12:23,170 --> 00:12:24,430
Sounds like corruption.

240
00:12:24,430 --> 00:12:26,090
They're digging their own graves

241
00:12:26,090 --> 00:12:26,870
by doing that.

242
00:12:27,550 --> 00:12:29,090
Should we try to report this?

243
00:12:29,430 --> 00:12:31,090
I wouldn't expect the Island Lord

244
00:12:31,090 --> 00:12:32,550
to come up with a good solution.

245
00:12:33,430 --> 00:12:34,590
Only rookies like Donnie

246
00:12:34,590 --> 00:12:35,730
would be affected by it.

247
00:12:36,390 --> 00:12:37,690
If the Island Lord burst

248
00:12:37,690 --> 00:12:38,710
after stuffing himself,

249
00:12:38,830 --> 00:12:39,830
I wouldn't mind at all.

250
00:12:39,990 --> 00:12:41,270
I'm pretty sure the Elves

251
00:12:41,270 --> 00:12:42,790
would step in and take his place.

252
00:12:43,150 --> 00:12:44,390
Yeah, so we still need him

253
00:12:44,390 --> 00:12:45,870
to act as sort of a middleman.

254
00:12:45,870 --> 00:12:48,910
We're dealing with a dwarf

255
00:12:48,910 --> 00:12:49,950
and a tall man

256
00:12:49,950 --> 00:12:52,030
and an elf and a half foot.

257
00:12:52,410 --> 00:12:53,430
What are you muttering?

258
00:12:53,850 --> 00:12:55,230
Those are the people in the party

259
00:12:55,230 --> 00:12:57,090
that put the ghost warding spell on us.

260
00:12:57,250 --> 00:12:59,090
Oh, the ones who stole our treasure.

261
00:12:59,350 --> 00:13:00,930
The ones who stole our food.

262
00:13:01,210 --> 00:13:02,550
There aren't very many parties

263
00:13:02,550 --> 00:13:03,450
with an elf in them.

264
00:13:03,790 --> 00:13:04,770
We might figure it out

265
00:13:04,770 --> 00:13:05,850
if we narrow things down.

266
00:13:06,850 --> 00:13:08,310
Maybe it's Donnie and Fiona?

267
00:13:09,030 --> 00:13:10,050
It's hard to believe

268
00:13:10,050 --> 00:13:11,090
that those two were able

269
00:13:11,090 --> 00:13:12,410
to make it to the third floor.

270
00:13:13,250 --> 00:13:15,590
Having only four party members is odd.

271
00:13:15,990 --> 00:13:17,390
It's more reckless than anything.

272
00:13:18,370 --> 00:13:19,570
Hey, Holm or Ren,

273
00:13:19,770 --> 00:13:21,710
look closer at this ghost-repelling spell.

274
00:13:22,230 --> 00:13:23,710
Wait, you still have that thing on?

275
00:13:23,930 --> 00:13:25,210
Well, yeah, it's evidence.

276
00:13:26,050 --> 00:13:28,390
That magic's not in my area of expertise.

277
00:13:29,610 --> 00:13:30,190
Let me see.

278
00:13:32,770 --> 00:13:33,370
Hmm.

279
00:13:34,750 --> 00:13:35,590
Honor student.

280
00:13:36,210 --> 00:13:37,050
It's like something

281
00:13:37,050 --> 00:13:38,270
